References: <18984188.8509.1255100905476.JavaMail.sfdc@na6-app1-7-sjl.ops.sfdc.net>
Message-ID: <8F89C5E3-2B68-45D3-A6C5-7FF92C3C587E@hudsonalpha.org>

Greetings

The latest version of the Illumina SCS software (v2.4) writes  
intensity files to network disk storage in separate folders for each  
cycle and without leading zeros, e.g., s_1_10.cif. The position files,  
however, do have leading zeros, e.g., s_1_0010_pos.txt. I checked the  
manuals and couldn't find a way to change one file name or the other  
and so I checked with Illumina and their response is below.

I think the best way to handle the difference WRT reading *.cif files  
in ShortRead is to make a list of all pos file names, delete the  
leading zeros, and then search that list with the pattern from  
readIntensities. Does that sound reasonable?

Cheers

Mike

